;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;--------------------------- INITIAL CYCLE ------------------------------------
;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;******************************************************************************
;
; This cycle is execute just once on start up, and it is the first
; execution module.
;
; Erase all possible:
;   Outputs, both local (L01 up to LO8) and remote (01 up to O1024).
;   Marks (M1 up to M8192) except those we want to memorise
;             (in this case M1 up to M99).
;   Register and counters except the first 20 (R1 up to R20, and C1 up to 20),
;             which can be set-up through machine parameters as non erasable.
;   Timmers (T1 up to T512).
;
; Set a mark called M_CY1 to "1" to use as a condition for first cycle
;   execution in the main PLC program module (PRG).
;
; The register called R_NULL is set to "0", to use in main PLC program
;   module (PRG).
;
;******************************************************************************
;                         EXCEPTIONS
;******************************************************************************
;
;#BEGIN EXCEPTIONS
;
; #Order number = 100
;
;#END EXCEPTIONS
;
CY1                             ; Beginning of first (initial) cycle
;
()                              ; Logic "1"
  = ERA O1 1024                 ; Output initialization
  = ERA LO1 8                   ; Output initialization locales
  = ERA M100 8192               ; Mark initialization
  = ERA R21 1024                ; Register initialization
  = ERA C021 256                ; Counter initialization
  = ERA T001 512                ; Timer initialization
  = SET M_CY1                   ; "first scan" bit
  = MOV 0 R_NULL                ; Register whose value is always zero
;
END
